      "reviews": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "gnanirahulnutakki"
            },
            "body": "I validated this at `94b638a45bf23d72e1249efff6c14adb0894a63e`. The implementation and targeted pre-commit checks are clean, but the new sample still has a label-set mismatch with the prompt-token vector, so the PR's stated PromQL expression remains empty without aggregation or explicit vector matching. I left one focused inline finding.",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "User",
                    "login": "gnanirahulnutakki"
                  },
                  "body": "The added zero series still cannot participate in the unmodified subtraction described in the PR. `prompt_tokens_total` is declared with only the base labels, while every `cached_tokens_total` child—including this one—also has `cache_source`; [PromQL's default one-to-one matching requires the exact same labels](https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/operators/#one-to-one-vector-matches), so `prompt_tokens_total - cached_tokens_total` continues to drop the series. Please either expose a separate aggregate counter with the base label set, or update the consumer query to aggregate this dimension first (for example, `prompt_tokens_total - sum without(cache_source) (cached_tokens_total)`). The test should cover that query-level behavior or at least assert the intended label compatibility; checking that a cached-token sample exists and sums to zero does not catch this mismatch.",
                  "createdAt": "2026-07-24T19:26:17Z",
                  "databaseId": 3647690927,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -1688,6 +1688,12 @@ def report_cache_source(source: str, value: int):\n                 # Fallback for backward compatibility\n                 labels_total = {**labels, \"cache_source\": \"total\"}\n                 self.cached_tokens_total.labels(**labels_total).inc(cached_tokens)\n+        else:\n+            # Register an explicit zero-valued series so PromQL expressions\n+            # combining prompt and cached-token counters retain this label set\n+            # before the first cache hit.\n+            labels_total = {**labels, \"cache_source\": \"total\"}",
                  "line": 1695,
                  "originalLine": 1695,
                  "path": "python/sglang/srt/observability/metrics_collector.py",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-24T19:26:24Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/32344#discussion_r3647690927"
                }
              ],
