  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "The added zero series still cannot participate in the unmodified subtraction described in the PR. `prompt_tokens_total` is declared with only the base labels, while every `cached_tokens_total` child—including this one—also has `cache_source`; [PromQL's default one-to-one matching requires the exact same labels](https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/operators/#one-to-one-vector-matches), so `prompt_tokens_total - cached_tokens_total` continues to drop the series. Please either expose a separate aggregate counter with the base label set, or update the consumer query to aggregate this dimension first (for example, `prompt_tokens_total - sum without(cache_source) (cached_tokens_total)`). The test should cover that query-level behavior or at least assert the intended label compatibility; checking that a cached-token sample exists and sums to zero does not catch this mismatch.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-24T19:26:17Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -1688,6 +1688,12 @@ def report_cache_source(source: str, value: int):\n                 # Fallback for backward compatibility\n                 labels_total = {**labels, \"cache_source\": \"total\"}\n                 self.cached_tokens_total.labels(**labels_total).inc(cached_tokens)\n+        else:\n+            # Register an explicit zero-valued series so PromQL expressions\n+            # combining prompt and cached-token counters retain this label set\n+            # before the first cache hit.\n+            labels_total = {**labels, \"cache_source\": \"total\"}",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/32344#discussion_r3647690927",
      "id": 3647690927,
